    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1067">

                <pb facs="1034" n="1022" xml:id="pg1022"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.00/170: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Agent and
                        Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Wadsworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-12T22:00:00-04:00">November 12,
                            1943—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>269. You should have no official relations with Edde regime, as per your 310,
                    November 11, noon.</p>
                <p>Sent to Beirut. Repeated to London, Cairo and Algiers for Murphy.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d1067-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1067-f1" n="26" xml:id="d1067-f1-content">
                <p>As telegrams Nos. 7141, 1730, and 2135, respectively.</p>
            </note>
